# Environment
@hosturl = http://localhost:4000
@xTenantId = local

### Stream remote CSV rows as JSON SSE events
# `url` must be an externally reachable HTTP(S) CSV URL.
# `batch-size` is optional and defaults to 100 (allowed range: 1-1000).
# `max-batches` is optional; when set, streaming stops after that many
# batches have been emitted (fires ACTION_COMPLETED early).
# Events use dff-util keys: PROCESSING, ACTION_COMPLETED, and OPERATION_FAILED.
# Every event payload has: processed, batches, data (valid records), and error
# (invalid record details or a fatal error code).
GET {{hosturl}}/csv-sse?url=https://dtf-boltnbolt-nprd.s3.ca-central-1.amazonaws.com/local/raghu/PRODUCT_AUTO.csv&batch-size=1&max-batches=1
Accept: text/event-stream
x-tenant-id: {{xTenantId}}

# For a terminal client use curl -N so it does not buffer SSE events:
# curl -N -H "x-tenant-id: local" "http://localhost:4000/csv-sse?url=https%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2Fdata.csv&batch-size=100"
